[292,293,294],"strong",{},"Docker"," with Compose, and at least 12 GB of memory available to it",[289,297,298,301,302],{},[292,299,300],{},"Bun",", from ",[303,304,308],"a",{"href":305,"rel":306},"https:\u002F\u002Fbun.sh",[307],"nofollow","bun.sh",[289,310,311,314,315,319],{},[292,312,313],{},"macOS on Apple silicon, or Linux with KVM"," (",[316,317,318],"code",{},"\u002Fdev\u002Fkvm","), where your apps' deployments run as micro VMs",[289,321,322,325],{},[292,323,324],{},"Claude Code",", which builds your app with the Kinotic plugin",[289,327,328],{},"An internet connection for the first start, which downloads Kinotic's images, and for each new project, whose starting code comes from GitHub",[330,331,333,337,387,407,411,418,468,471,475,483,487],"steps",{"level":332},"4",[281,334,336],{"id":335},"install-and-launch-kinotic","Install and launch Kinotic",[338,339,344],"pre",{"className":340,"code":341,"language":342,"meta":343,"style":343},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","git clone https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic.git\ncd kinotic\u002Fdeployment\u002Fdocker-compose\ndocker compose up -d\n","bash","",[316,345,346,362,372],{"__ignoreMap":343},[347,348,351,355,359],"span",{"class":349,"line":350},"line",1,[347,352,354],{"class":353},"sBMFI","git",[347,356,358],{"class":357},"sfazB"," clone",[347,360,361],{"class":357}," https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic.git\n",[347,363,365,369],{"class":349,"line":364},2,[347,366,368],{"class":367},"s2Zo4","cd",[347,370,371],{"class":357}," kinotic\u002Fdeployment\u002Fdocker-compose\n",[347,373,375,378,381,384],{"class":349,"line":374},3,[347,376,377],{"class":353},"docker",[347,379,380],{"class":357}," compose",[347,382,383],{"class":357}," up",[347,385,386],{"class":357}," -d\n",[265,388,389,390,394,395,398,399,402,403,406],{},"The first start downloads the images and prepares the database, which takes a few minutes. The portal\nopens at ",[303,391,392],{"href":392,"rel":393},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090",[307]," once ",[316,396,397],{},"docker compose ps"," lists the three\n",[316,400,401],{},"kinotic-server-*"," containers as ",[316,404,405],{},"healthy",".",[281,408,410],{"id":409},"start-the-node-that-runs-your-deployments","Start the node that runs your deployments",[265,412,413,414,417],{},"Every push to a project deploys it onto a node on your machine. In another terminal, from the folder you\nran ",[316,415,416],{},"git clone"," in:",[338,419,421],{"className":340,"code":420,"language":342,"meta":343,"style":343},"cd kinotic\u002Fkinotic-js\u002Fworkspace\nbun install && bun run build\ncd packages\u002Fvm-manager\nbun run dev\n",[316,422,423,430,451,458],{"__ignoreMap":343},[347,424,425,427],{"class":349,"line":350},[347,426,368],{"class":367},[347,428,429],{"class":357}," kinotic\u002Fkinotic-js\u002Fworkspace\n",[347,431,432,435,438,442,445,448],{"class":349,"line":364},[347,433,434],{"class":353},"bun",[347,436,437],{"class":357}," install",[347,439,441],{"class":440},"sMK4o"," &&",[347,443,444],{"class":353}," bun",[347,446,447],{"class":357}," run",[347,449,450],{"class":357}," build\n",[347,452,453,455],{"class":349,"line":374},[347,454,368],{"class":367},[347,456,457],{"class":357}," packages\u002Fvm-manager\n",[347,459,461,463,465],{"class":349,"line":460},4,[347,462,434],{"class":353},[347,464,447],{"class":357},[347,466,467],{"class":357}," dev\n",[265,469,470],{},"Leave it running; it connects to Kinotic and takes each deployment as it comes.",[281,472,474],{"id":473},"create-your-organization","Create your organization",[265,476,477,478,482],{},"Open ",[303,479,480],{"href":480,"rel":481},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090\u002Fsignup",[307],", enter your name and email, then name\nyour organization and set a password. A local install sends no email, so the page goes straight on, and\nyou are signed in to your new organization.",[281,484,486],{"id":485},"follow-the-quickstart-in-the-portal","Follow the Quickstart in the portal",[265,488,477,489,491],{},[292,490,5],{}," in the portal's sidebar. It walks you through installing the Kinotic plugin in Claude\nCode, connecting Claude to your local Kinotic, and asking for your app. Claude creates the application\nand its project, writes the entities, services and UIs, and pushes to the project's repository; every\npush deploys.",[265,493,494,497,498,501,502,505,506,509],{},[316,495,496],{},"docker compose stop"," stops Kinotic and keeps your data for the next ",[316,499,500],{},"docker compose up -d",";\n",[316,503,504],{},"docker compose down -v"," deletes it. ",[303,507,508],{"href":209},"Developing Kinotic"," covers what the\nstack runs and how to work on Kinotic itself.",[273,511,514],{"icon":512,"label":513},"i-lucide-cloud","Cloud",[515,516],"cloud-waitlist",{},[518,519,521],"h2",{"id":520},"whats-next","What's Next?",[265,523,524],{},"Once your first app is deployed, explore the rest of the documentation:",[286,526,527,533,538],{},[289,528,529,532],{},[303,530,531],{"href":52},"Application Structure"," -- Understand how organizations, applications, projects, and artifacts are organized.",[289,534,535,537],{},[303,536,63],{"href":69}," -- Learn how to publish and consume services across your application.",[289,539,540,542],{},[303,541,84],{"href":90}," -- Dive deeper into entity definitions, relationships, and querying.",[544,545,546],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decor